Repo: <workspace> (Hono 4.13.18). Work only in this repo; do not commit, stage, or create branches.

TASK: Fix the Set-Cookie merge bug in Context's `res` setter in `src/context.ts` (currently ~lines 414-434), and add/update tests in `src/context.test.ts`.

CURRENT BUGGY CODE:
```ts
  set res(_res: Response | undefined) {
    if (this.#res && _res) {
      _res = createResponseInstance(_res.body, _res)
      for (const [k, v] of this.#res.headers.entries()) {
        if (k === 'content-type') {
          continue
        }
        if (k === 'set-cookie') {
          const cookies = this.#res.headers.getSetCookie()
          _res.headers.delete('set-cookie')
          for (const cookie of cookies) {
            _res.headers.append('set-cookie', cookie)
          }
        } else {
          _res.headers.set(k, v)
        }
      }
    }
    this.#res = _res
    this.finalized = true
  }
```
Bug: when middleware already set cookies on `c.res`, and a handler returns a new Response that has its own `Set-Cookie`, the `_res.headers.delete('set-cookie')` drops the handler's cookie(s). Both must survive. Note: `this.#res.headers.entries()` yields one entry per Set-Cookie value, so do NOT append old cookies inside that loop (would duplicate them when there are multiple old cookies).

REQUIRED FIX (adapt exactly, keep style/formatting consistent with the repo):
```ts
  set res(_res: Response | undefined) {
    if (this.#res && _res) {
      _res = createResponseInstance(_res.body, _res)
      const previousCookies = this.#res.headers.getSetCookie()
      for (const [k, v] of this.#res.headers.entries()) {
        if (k === 'content-type' || k === 'set-cookie') {
          continue
        }
        _res.headers.set(k, v)
      }
      if (previousCookies.length > 0) {
        const newCookies = _res.headers.getSetCookie()
        _res.headers.delete('set-cookie')
        for (const cookie of previousCookies) {
          _res.headers.append('set-cookie', cookie)
        }
        for (const cookie of newCookies) {
          _res.headers.append('set-cookie', cookie)
        }
      }
    }
    this.#res = _res
    this.finalized = true
  }
```
This preserves old cookies first, then the new response's cookies, and non-set-cookie headers still override as before. Do not change unrelated behavior.

TESTS in `src/context.test.ts`:
1. Existing test "Should set cookie headers when re-assigning Response to `c.res`" (around lines 430-445) currently asserts the buggy behavior: after re-assigning a response with `foo3=bar3`, it expects only the two old cookies. Update its last two assertions to expect the merged list in order:
```ts
    expect(c.res.headers.getSetCookie().length).toBe(cookies.length + newCookies.length)
    expect(c.res.headers.getSetCookie()).toEqual([...cookies, ...newCookies])
```
2. Add a new regression test inside the `describe('Context header', ...)` block (after the existing cookie tests, around line 454), covering the middleware + handler scenario:
```ts
  it('Should keep a Set-Cookie header from a new Response when a cookie is already set on c.res', () => {
    // Middleware has already set a cookie on the response
    c.res.headers.append('set-cookie', 'middleware=1; Path=/')

    // Handler returns a new Response with its own cookie
    const handlerResponse = new Response('ok', {
      headers: [['set-cookie', 'handler=1; Path=/']],
    })
    c.res = handlerResponse

    expect(c.res.headers.getSetCookie()).toEqual([
      'middleware=1; Path=/',
      'handler=1; Path=/',
    ])
  })
```
Feel free to improve the test name/comments slightly, but the scenario and assertions must remain.

VERIFY: run `pnpm exec vp test --run src/context.test.ts` from the repo root and confirm ALL tests pass (baseline was 63 passed; should be 64 after adding one test). If any other test in that file fails, report it rather than papering over it.

REPORT BACK: the exact diff (git diff) for both files, the test command output summary (test files/tests passed), and any concerns. Do not run git add/commit.

